  "question": {
    "text": "Reaction of thionyl chloride with white phosphorus forms a compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>]</mo></math>, which on hydrolysis gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>]</mo></math>, a dibasic acid. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>]</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>]</mo></math> are respectively"
